'''Maridun''' was a [[planet]] located in the [[Rolion sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. It was a temperate and verdant world, with a comfortable climate despite its challenging ecosystem and dangerous [[Diet|predators]]. Covered in [[grass]]y plains where large seed pods grew, it was the homeworld of the [[Amani]]n and was inhabited by [[mastiff phalone]]s.

==Description==
In its eponymous [[Maridun system|star system]] in the [[Rolion sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> at grid Q-6 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="TFABG" /> the [[planet]] Maridun was the very definition of unassuming. A world of gently undulating terrain covered in rolling [[grass]]lands, Maridun survived largely unscathed throughout [[The galaxy|galactic]] history due to what little it had to provide offworld industry. In contrast to other planets like [[Lothal]], Maridun had no resources worth mining from the surface, and instead, had seemingly endless quantities of grass.<ref name="BMF 88">{{BuildFalconCite|88|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref>

Maridun maintained a breathable [[atmosphere]]<ref name="DoP" /> as well as a [[Temperature|temperate]] climate, despite its challenging ecosystem and dangerous [[Diet|predators]].<ref name="VE" /> On the surface, the grasses of Maridun grew high, to the point where they could tower over two [[meter]]s tall. The planet's grasslands were interspersed with enormous [[tree]]s, in areas where [[water]] reserves were closest to the surface. Thick and deep-rooted, each tree was up of others that grew close by and merged with the main tree over [[time]].<ref name="BMF 88" /> The [[Amani]] lived on the world and hunted the [[Charnoq]]s.<ref name="Mustafar and Other Outer Rim Planets" /> Dangerous [[mastiff phalone]]s lived in the fields.<ref name="JC" />

==History==
[[Lurmen]] refugees who sought to escape the [[Clone Wars]] settled on the planet,<ref name="JC" /> seeking to make peaceful new lives away from watchful [[eye]]s.<ref name="VE" /> During the war, [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] survivors of the [[Battle of Quell]] crash-landed there and discovered the [[Lurmen village]].<ref name="JC" /> Soon, [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[General]] [[Lok Durd]] arrived and sought an alliance with the Lurmen, while plotting to test a new weapon known as the [[Defoliator]] on them. The [[Jedi]] present discovered this and [[Defense of Maridun|defended the Lurmen village]] when Durd betrayed them. They rallied the villagers, disabled the Defoliator and captured Durd before three [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|Star Destroyers]] arrived to retrieve them.<ref name="DoP" />

